# MAP (ray numbers on the source grid) and RAY (one ray, surface by surface) on the manual's
# Cassegrain with exit pupil (cmdref: Ray Tracing).  The chief ray (1) is not shown by MAP; RAY 1
# reports it obscured by element 1 (the secondary's shadow) and still traces it to the detector;
# the Return-1 -> ExitPupil leg has a NEGATIVE segment length (the return reverses the beam).
old $ROOT/docs/macos-manual/examples/CassWithExitPupil.in
map
ray
1
0
# EXPECT: Map of rays at input aperture
# EXPECT: 0   0   0   0 120 121 122 123 124 125   0
# EXPECT: Ray\s+1 is the chief ray\.
# EXPECT: Ray\s+1 is obscured by element\s+1
# EXPECT: to Element\s+4 \(Return1\s*\):[\s\S]*?Total Length=\s+1\.46222918040000D\+01
# EXPECT: to Element\s+5 \(ExitPupil\s*\):[\s\S]*?Segment Length= -5\.56014590200000D\+00
# EXPECT: to Element\s+6 \(Detector\s*\)
# EXPECT-NOT: forrtl
